name: php-agent-devdescription: >-  Token-efficient, bug-resistant PHP development workflow for AI coding  agents. Covers Laravel, Symfony, WordPress, CodeIgniter and plain PHP.  Use when starting any PHP coding task or project, when creating agent  context files (AGENTS.md, PLAN.md, DECISIONS.md), when exploring a PHP  codebase, or when the user mentions saving tokens, reducing costs, or  improving quality on a PHP project.
PHP Agent Development — token-efficient workflow

Core principle: every token either moves the task forward or preventsfuture waste. PHP projects contain the largest context traps of anylanguage (vendor/, framework caches, WordPress core) — hygiene mattersmore here than anywhere.
Phase 0 — BOOTSTRAP (once per project)

    Detect the stack before anything else:

Signal	Stack
composer.json → laravel/framework	Laravel
composer.json → symfony/framework-bundle	Symfony
wp-config.php / wp-settings.php exists	WordPress
composer.json → codeigniter4/framework	CodeIgniter 4
none of the above	plain PHP

Command sets per stack: references/php-commands.md.

    Create AGENTS.md in the repo root — the project brain every sessionreads first. Copy the matching template fromreferences/agents-md-templates.md. Keep ≤ 150 lines; update wheneverarchitecture changes.

    Mark the no-read zone (the #1 PHP token sink) in AGENTS.md hardrules and in .claudeignore / deny rules where supported:vendor/ · node_modules/ · composer.lock · storage/framework/ ·bootstrap/cache/ · var/cache/ · public/build/ · dist/ ·_ide_helper*.php · .phpstorm.meta.php · *.min.js · *.min.css · *.map ·uploads/ · WordPress: wp-admin/ · wp-includes/ · wp-content/uploads/(WP core: grep one specific symbol only when debugging a hook;never bulk-read, never edit.)

    Confirm test-one / lint / typecheck commands actually run; recordthem in AGENTS.md.

Phase 1 — PLAN

Non-trivial tasks (touch > 1 file or > 50 lines) get PLAN.md first(references/plan-templates.md):

    one-sentence goal + checkable acceptance criteria
    target files — found via AGENTS.md map or route:list, NOT exploration
    ordered atomic steps
    DB plan: new migration vs editing old (executed migrations are immutable)
    out-of-scope list (blocks gold-plating)

Trivial fixes (typo, text string, one-line config) skip planning.
Phase 2 — EXECUTE (PHP context economy)

    Locate with grep, read ranges only:grep -rn --include="*.php" "functionName" app/ → sed -n '40,120p' fileNever cat whole large files.
    Get an API surface almost free:grep -n "public function" app/Services/Foo.php prints the interface.
    Explore with commands, not file reads (near-zero token cost):php artisan route:list · php artisan model:show User ·php bin/console debug:router · composer show vendor/pkg ·composer why pkg — full list in references/php-commands.md.
    Vendor code: read only the docblock/signature of the class beingused, never implementation internals. Prefer reflection in tinker:(new ReflectionClass(Foo::class))->getMethods().
    Never edit: vendor/ (fork/upgrade instead), framework core,generated files, already-executed migrations, composer.lock by hand.
    DB schema changes → fresh migration; record its name in DECISIONS.md.
    After config/route/env changes → clear caches before testing:php artisan optimize:clear (or bin/console cache:clear).Stale caches cause phantom bugs and wasted debug loops.
    Surgical edits: change only the lines that change. One class per file(PSR-4) keeps files small — keep them that way.
    Subagents for multi-file exploration; main context keeps only summaries.

Phase 3 — VERIFY (targeted, not exhaustive)

    Tests covering the change only:vendor/bin/phpunit --filter testMethodName · vendor/bin/pest --filter name· php artisan test --filter=Name. Full suite only before commit/PR.
    Static analysis on changed paths (seconds, zero tokens, real bugs):vendor/bin/phpstan analyse <changed paths> --level=8 (or Psalm).
    Style on dirty files only: vendor/bin/pint --dirty (or phpcbf).
    php -l <file> on every changed file — free fatal-error check.
    Smoke test: start server, curl the one affected endpoint.
    Grep for debug leftovers before commit:grep -rn "dd(\|dump(\|var_dump(\|ray(" app/
    Done = every acceptance criterion checked one by one.

Fix failures immediately — context is warm; a later debug session reloadseverything.
Phase 4 — PERSIST

    Update AGENTS.md (status, map changes, new commands).
    Mark PLAN.md steps; log deviations.
    DECISIONS.md one-liners: non-obvious choices, new composer deps,migration names, hook changes (WP).
    Conventional commit: feat|fix|refactor: what + why — git history isfree persistent context.
    New task → fresh session; resume from files, not from memory.

Universal rules

    Consult order: AGENTS.md → PLAN.md → DECISIONS.md → code.
    Never redo what progress files say is done.
    migrate:fresh / db:wipe / migrate:reset = data loss → explicituser approval, dev environments only.
    Never commit .env or wp-config.php with real credentials (.env.exampleis the pattern).
    New code: strict_types + full typing (see references/php-conventions.md).
    Ambiguous → ask. Confident → act. Never silently guess architecture.

📄 references/php-commands.md
PHP command cheat sheet (per stack)
Plain PHP (works everywhere)

    Free fatal check: php -l path/File.php
    Dev server: php -S localhost:8000 -t public
    Composer: composer install · composer dump-autoload -o ·composer show vendor/pkg (version + description) · composer why pkg· composer outdated --direct
    PHPUnit: vendor/bin/phpunit --filter=testName tests/Unit/FooTest.php(also --testsuite=Unit)
    PHPStan: vendor/bin/phpstan analyse src --level=8
    Psalm: vendor/bin/psalm src
    Find a class: grep -rn --include="*.php" "class Foo" src/

Laravel

    Run: php artisan serve
    Routes: php artisan route:list --path=api/users
    Explore (REPL): php artisan tinker
        Schema::getColumnListing('users') — schema without reading migrations
        (new ReflectionClass(User::class))->getMethods()
    Model map: php artisan model:show User
    Tests: php artisan test --filter=Name · --group=api ·parallel: php artisan test --parallel
    Migrations: php artisan make:migration add_x_to_y_table ·php artisan migrate · php artisan migrate:rollback --step=1· DESTRUCTIVE: migrate:fresh --seed — approval only
    Caches: php artisan optimize:clear (config+routes+views+events)
    Queue: php artisan queue:restart after Job changes · queue:failed
    Logs: tail -n 50 storage/logs/laravel.log
    Style (changed files only): vendor/bin/pint --dirty
    Types: vendor/bin/phpstan analyse app --level=8 (larastan)

Symfony

    php bin/console list · php bin/console debug:router ·debug:router <name> · debug:container --parameter=x
    php bin/console cache:clear --env=dev
    Doctrine migrations: doctrine:migrations:diff · doctrine:migrations:migrate
    Tests: php bin/phpunit --filter testName
    Serve: symfony serve (Symfony CLI) or php -S localhost:8000 -t public

WordPress (wp-cli)

    Site: wp plugin list · wp theme list · wp option get siteurl
    Data: wp search-replace 'old' 'new' --dry-run · wp db check
    Reflection: wp eval 'var_dump(class_exists("WC_Order"));'
    Debug: WP_DEBUG=true in wp-config.php → wp-content/debug.log
    Assets: npm run build / npm run dev (theme/plugin package.json)

CodeIgniter 4

    php spark serve · php spark routes · php spark migrate
    Tests: vendor/bin/phpunit

The golden habit

Always target: one test, one class, one file. Whole suites only pre-PR.
📄 references/php-conventions.md
PHP conventions — bug prevention = token prevention

Every bug avoided removes a whole debug loop (read, hypothesize, edit,retest) — the most expensive token sequence there is. Apply to NEW code;never mass-refactor old code unprompted.
Typing (PHP 8.1+)

    declare(strict_types=1); in every new file
    Type every property, parameter and return — mixed only when truly dynamic
    readonly properties/classes for value objects
    Backed enums instead of string/int constant soup
    Nullable only where the domain allows, never "just in case"
    Dedicated DTOs at boundaries instead of array-shape juggling

Structure

    PSR-4: one class per file, namespace mirrors path
    final by default; inheritance only by design
    Files < 300 lines, methods < 30 lines (small files are cheap to re-read)
    Layers: Controller (thin: validate + delegate) → Action/Service →Model/Repository
    Constructor property promotion; inject dependencies; no service locator
    Throw typed exceptions; never return mixed "error or value"
    Early returns; no deep nesting

Laravel specifics

    FormRequest for validation — never inline in controllers
    Business logic in Actions/Services; controllers ≤ ~30 lines
    Eloquent: query scopes for repeated filters; with() eager loads to kill N+1
    Route model binding over manual findOrFail
    Migrations reversible (down()); one concern per migration
    Factories + RefreshDatabase in tests; never manual SQL seeding
    Values via config() — never scattered hardcoded env values

WordPress specifics

    Prefix ALL global symbols with the theme/plugin slug:mytheme_render_card(), Mytheme_Meta_Box, mytheme_after_content
    Output escaping non-negotiable: esc_html esc_attr esc_url wp_kses_post· input: sanitize_text_field absint · SQL: $wpdb->prepare()
    Register hooks in ONE bootstrap file; keep a hook map in AGENTS.md
    Never modify core / parent theme / other plugins — hooks only
    Nonces for any state change: wp_nonce_field() / check_admin_referer()
    No raw $_GET/$_POST/$_SERVER in templates — sanitize and validate first
    i18n-ready: __('text', 'mytheme')

Hard NO list

    committing dd() dump() var_dump() ray() (grep before commit)
    editing an executed migration
    @ error suppression · eval() · extract() · die() flow control
    editing vendor/ to "quick-fix" a package (fork/patch via composer instead)
    queries in views/templates
    hardcoded credentials anywhere (env only)

