AGENTS.md templates (pick ONE matching the detected stack)
A) Laravel
AGENTS.md — [Project] (Laravel 11)
Purpose

[1–2 sentences: what this app does, for whom.]
Stack

PHP 8.3 · Laravel 11 · MySQL 8 · Redis (cache+queue) · Pest · Larastan · Pint
Map & flow

    routes/web.php, routes/api.php — route table
    app/Http/Controllers/* — thin controllers (validate → delegate → respond)
    app/Http/Requests/* — form validation
    app/Actions/* — business logic units (one action = one job)
    app/Models/* — Eloquent models + query scopes
    app/Services/* — external integrations (payment, sms, mail)
    app/Jobs/, app/Events/, app/Listeners/ — async side
    database/migrations|factories|seeders/
    tests/Feature/, tests/Unit/ (Pest)
    Flow: request → middleware → FormRequest → Controller → Action → Model→ MySQL · events → Redis queue → Job → listener

Commands

    bootstrap: composer install && cp .env.example .env && php artisan key:generate && php artisan migrate --seed
    serve: php artisan serve
    test all: php artisan test
    test one: php artisan test --filter=Name
    style: vendor/bin/pint --dirty
    types: vendor/bin/phpstan analyse --level=8
    explore: php artisan route:list / tinker / model:show User

Conventions

strict_types · final classes · DTOs for API payloads · Actions pattern ·singular models, snake_case tables
Hard rules (NEVER)

    migrate:fresh / db:wipe → user approval, dev DB only
    never edit vendor/ or any already-committed migration
    never commit .env; never leave dd()/dump()
    queue runs on Redis: php artisan queue:restart after Job changes
    after config/route changes run php artisan optimize:clear

Current status

    done: … · in progress: … (see PLAN.md) · known issues: …

